    "reasoning": "All 15 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. No prior submission or grade is supplied; confirmation rests on the worked solutions. q-124105: applying T to P=(-1,1) and Q=(2,-1) gives P'=(0,0) and Q'=(-8,-1), matching option 4. q-124641: the rectangle's vertices (0,0),(1,0),(1,2),(0,2) map to (1,1),(3,2),(1,0),(-1,-1), matching option 2. The solution calls the rectangle a 'square'; this terminology error does not affect its calculation or answer. q-124343: T(u,v)=(1-v,1+u) maps the triangle's vertices to (0,1),(0,3),(-1,3), matching option 0. q-162175 and q-162172: area scale factors are absolute determinants, |2+1|=3 and |-2-3|=5; translations do not affect area. q-34247: x=(b-3a)/2=(6,7,-6,-1), so x1+x2=13. q-105157: x=(b-2a)/4=(1,2,-1,-3). For each horizontal parabola use (y-k)^2=C(x-h), with C determined by its given point. q-115627: C=9/(-2)=-9/2. q-115602: C=9/1=9. q-11753: C=16/8=2. q-11765: C=64/12=16/3. q-11809: vertex (-6,0) gives C=36/4=9. q-115643: vertex (0,-3) gives C=9/3=3. q-11802: vertex (5,1) gives C=16/(-6)=-8/3. q-11812: vertex (-4,-3) gives C=25/5=5. Each equation has the required vertex, opening direction, and supplied point.",
